# Tests travel with the code

Every crate change that can fail in production gets a test in the same
change. Do not leave “we will test it on the box” as the only check.

## WebAPI and other external dialects

When a server replies in a way we did not model, **paste that body into a
test** (redact secrets and hostnames). Then make the client accept it.

The qBittorrent 5.2.3 `torrents/add` JSON
(`success_count` / `added_torrent_ids`) looked like success on the wire
and FAIL in `tsync import` because the fixture still used `204` + empty
or `Ok.`. That class of bug is a missing fixture, not a missing manual run.

## What “done” means

- Unit or fake-server test covers the new branch.
- A wrong assumption in an existing fake (legacy-only reply) is updated,
  not left as the sole 5.x stand-in.
- `cargo test` for the touched crate passes before you move on.
